{"base_rate":0.43915343915343913,"brier":0.1391664021164021,"bss":0.43496669129347587,"bss_hi":0.5142206316571479,"bss_lo":0.35346431801093003,"chart":{"base":[631.4,53.1],"fp":[231.3,299.7],"lead":"62,261 272,236.7 482,186.2 692,113.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.43 — higher than 83% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +16pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 66% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 6%; promised 97% → rained 82%"},"rel":"81.8,438.6 382.8,282.5 671,112.4"},"country":"DE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09246031746031749,"ess":375.8755512766777,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Koeln</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Koeln rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>84%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 756 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nKOLN-BONN, 16.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.43, ranked 37 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(17&ndash;75) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>222</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>35%</td><td class='num'><b>37%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'><b>48%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>74%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>84%</b></td><td class='num'>231</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Koeln</b> <span class=\"muted\">Germany</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.43</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>17&ndash;75\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>756 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Koeln &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Koeln\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.66972972972973,378.72072072072075 98.89153846153846,316.6666666666667 182.50552631578947,219.03815789473748 293.2490909090909,103.09090909090907 368.045,38.22222222222223 410.207012987013,18.0 410.207012987013,24.30303030303031 368.045,93.83333333333337 293.2490909090909,178.72727272727275 182.50552631578947,291.0 98.89153846153846,363.3333333333333 58.66972972972973,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"222.14814814814815\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"222.14814814814815\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.66972972972973,373.8018018018018 98.89153846153846,316.6666666666667 182.50552631578947,247.89473684210526 293.2490909090909,207.0909090909091 368.045,114.05555555555554 410.207012987013,74.72727272727275\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 222 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.66972972972973\" cy=\"373.8018018018018\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"98.89153846153846\" cy=\"316.6666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 35%&amp;#10;It rained 37% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"182.50552631578947\" cy=\"247.89473684210526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 66%&amp;#10;It rained 48% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"293.2490909090909\" cy=\"207.0909090909091\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 74% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"368.045\" cy=\"114.05555555555554\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 84% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 231 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.207012987013\" cy=\"74.72727272727275\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(44%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Koeln the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.55) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.34).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'>0.335</td><td class='num'>10.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.392</td><td class='num'>11.0%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'>0.409</td><td class='num'>8.4%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>0.547</td><td class='num'>7.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":50.93333,"lon":6.95,"n":756,"n_cities":213,"name":"Koeln","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.001891891891891892,"n":222,"obs":0.02252252252252252,"sig":true},{"hi":0.23,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.11551282051282051,"n":78,"obs":0.1794871794871795,"sig":false},{"hi":0.51,"lo":0.23,"mean":0.3517105263157895,"n":76,"obs":0.3684210526315789